IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `spr-part5-sharing`

-- Tests for Part 5: the regulation 6 that paragraph 1(10) of the Schedule inserts (lines 545 to 566).
-- Durations follow fork F7: "three months beginning with" a day ends the day before the same day three months on;
-- "six weeks beginning with" a day ends 41 days after it.

§ `Part 5`

GIVEN received IS A DATE
      relevant IS A MAYBE DATE
      includes IS A BOOLEAN
      notified IS A BOOLEAN
      court IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Request for information about sharing`
`a request` received relevant includes notified court MEANS
    `Request for information about sharing` WITH
        `the date the Secretary of State receives the request or the order` IS received
        `the relevant date` IS relevant
        `the request or order includes a valuation under paragraphs (2), (3) or (4) or an amount under paragraph (5)` IS includes
        `the person notified the Secretary of State by then that the information is needed in connection with proceedings` IS notified
        `the last day of a shorter period specified by the court in an order` IS court

`valuation now` MEANS `a valuation of the shareable new state scheme rights as at the date the request is received`
`valuation at relevant date` MEANS `a valuation of the shareable new state scheme rights as at the relevant date`
`old rights valuation` MEANS `a valuation of the previous shareable old state scheme rights as at the relevant date`
`category A amount` MEANS `the amount of the former entitlement to a category A retirement pension by virtue of section 44(3)(b) of the 1992 Act, as at the relevant date and immediately before 6 April 2016`
`explanation` MEANS `an explanation of the shareable new state scheme rights, of the effect of a pension sharing order or provision, of how the spouse or civil partner becomes entitled, and of how that differs from shared additional pension`

§§ `Inserted regulation 6(2) to (6): what is furnished`

-- (2) the default: a valuation as at the date the request is received; (6) the explanation; always.
#ASSERT `the information the person with shareable new state scheme rights is owed on request` (`a request` (Date 1 6 2026) NOTHING TRUE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS LIST `valuation now`, `explanation`
-- (3) the relevant date is on or after 6 April 2016: a valuation as at the relevant date.
#ASSERT `the information the person with shareable new state scheme rights is owed on request` (`a request` (Date 1 6 2026) (JUST (Date 10 5 2017)) TRUE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS LIST `valuation at relevant date`, `explanation`
#ASSERT `the information the person with shareable new state scheme rights is owed on request` (`a request` (Date 1 6 2026) (JUST (Date 6 4 2016)) TRUE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS LIST `valuation at relevant date`, `explanation`
-- (4) and (5) the relevant date is before 6 April 2016 and the request is received on or after it: the old rights, and the amount.
#ASSERT `the information the person with shareable new state scheme rights is owed on request` (`a request` (Date 1 6 2026) (JUST (Date 1 3 2016)) TRUE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS LIST `old rights valuation`, `category A amount`, `explanation`
#ASSERT `the information the person with shareable new state scheme rights is owed on request` (`a request` (Date 6 4 2016) (JUST (Date 5 4 2016)) TRUE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS LIST `old rights valuation`, `category A amount`, `explanation`
-- (8)(a) a request that includes no valuation or amount: the explanation only.
#ASSERT `the information the person with shareable new state scheme rights is owed on request` (`a request` (Date 1 6 2026) (JUST (Date 10 5 2017)) FALSE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS LIST `explanation`
-- (1)(b) the spouse or civil partner is owed the explanation in (6).
#ASSERT `the information the spouse or civil partner of the person is owed on request` EQUALS LIST `explanation`

§§ `Inserted regulation 6(7) and (8): by when`

-- (7)(a) three months beginning with 1 March 2026: to 31 May.
#ASSERT `the last day by which the Secretary of State must furnish the information` (`a request` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING TRUE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS Date 31 5 2026
-- (7)(b) six weeks beginning with 1 March 2026, if the person has so notified: to 11 April.
#ASSERT `the last day by which the Secretary of State must furnish the information` (`a request` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING TRUE TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS Date 11 4 2026
-- (7)(c) a shorter period the court specifies: the earliest that applies.
#ASSERT `the last day by which the Secretary of State must furnish the information` (`a request` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING TRUE TRUE (JUST (Date 20 3 2026))) EQUALS Date 20 3 2026
#ASSERT `the last day by which the Secretary of State must furnish the information` (`a request` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING TRUE FALSE (JUST (Date 20 3 2026))) EQUALS Date 20 3 2026
-- A court period that is not shorter does not extend the time.
#ASSERT `the last day by which the Secretary of State must furnish the information` (`a request` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING TRUE FALSE (JUST (Date 15 7 2026))) EQUALS Date 31 5 2026
-- (8) one month beginning with the day received.
#ASSERT `the last day by which the Secretary of State must furnish the information` (`a request` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS Date 31 3 2026
#ASSERT `the last day by which the Secretary of State must furnish the information` (`a request` (Date 31 1 2026) NOTHING FALSE FALSE NOTHING) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
-- (8) does not take the six-week or court periods: they belong to paragraph (7).
#ASSERT `the last day by which the Secretary of State must furnish the information` (`a request` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING FALSE TRUE NOTHING) EQUALS Date 31 3 2026
